'''Genètica de l'Istme, S.L.''' is a Balboan {{w|agricultural biotechnology}} company based at [[Plastic Beach]] in [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], [[Sant Cristòfor]]. The company develops crop varieties adapted to the Balboan climate, focusing on drought tolerance, disease resistance, and improved yields for crops grown in the country's diverse agricultural regions. Founded in 2023 as a spin-off from the [[University of Sant Cristòfor]]'s biochemical research programme at Plastic Beach, Genètica de l'Istme is one of the newest companies in the Dàrsena research cluster.

== History ==

=== Founding (2023) ===

Genètica de l'Istme was founded in 2023 by Dr. Marta Vergés i Puig and Dr. Oriol Bosch i Riera, researchers from the [[University of Sant Cristòfor]]'s biochemical research building at [[Plastic Beach]]. Vergés, a plant geneticist, had been researching {{w|marker-assisted selection}} and {{w|genomic selection}} techniques for tropical crops at the university, with a focus on adapting crops to the varied Balboan growing conditions — from the humid Migjorn lowlands to the drier Tramuntana savanna. Bosch, an agricultural scientist, had worked on disease resistance in coffee and cacao at the university's agricultural research station in the [[Jala Province|Jala]] highlands before joining the Plastic Beach facility.

The two researchers identified a gap between the university's crop genetics research and its application in Balboan agriculture. While the university produced research on crop adaptation, the country's agricultural sector — dominated by cooperative farms growing coffee, sugar cane, bananas, cacao, and rice — had limited access to improved varieties suited to local conditions. Imported varieties from [[Tapuya]] and [[Sinchew]] were not always adapted to Balboan soil types, rainfall patterns, or pest pressures, and the overvalued [[International Dollar]] made imported seed expensive.

The company was established as a private limited company ({{lang|ca|Societat Limitada}}, S.L.) with seed funding from the [[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] (FIDB) and the University of Sant Cristòfor Investment Fund. [[Nutrició del Món]] (NDM), the state-owned fertiliser and agricultural inputs company, took a 20 per cent strategic stake, reflecting its interest in crop improvement as a complement to its fertiliser business. The founders retained 35 per cent, with the remaining 15 per cent held by venture capital investors.

=== Early research (2023–present) ===

Genètica de l'Istme's initial research programme focuses on three crop areas:

* '''Coffee''': Developing disease-resistant varieties for the [[Jala Province|Jala]] highlands, where {{w|coffee leaf rust}} ({{lang|ca|roya del cafè}}) and {{w|coffee berry disease}} periodically reduce yields on cooperative farms. The company uses marker-assisted selection to identify resistance genes in existing Balboan coffee germplasm and cross them with high-yielding varieties, avoiding the regulatory and public acceptance issues associated with {{w|genetically modified organism|transgenic approaches}}.
* '''Sugar cane and rice''': Developing drought-tolerant varieties for the [[Migjorn Province|Migjorn]] lowlands, where rainfall variability affects yields on cooperative and commercial farms. The company's Migjorn varieties are designed to maintain yields during dry periods without requiring additional irrigation, reducing the water footprint of sugar and rice production.
* '''Cacao''': Developing varieties resistant to {{w|frosty pod rot}} and {{w|black pod disease}} for the Jala highlands and Migjorn lowlands, where cacao is grown by cooperative farms. Cacao diseases have been a recurring problem for Balboan producers, and improved varieties could reduce crop losses and stabilise incomes for cooperative farmers.

The company operates from a converted warehouse at Plastic Beach, using the cluster's shared laboratory facilities and the university's genomic sequencing equipment. The proximity to the university's biochemical research building provides access to graduate researchers and analytical infrastructure. Field trials are conducted in partnership with cooperative farms in Jala and Migjorn, and with [[Corporació Agrícola de l'Istme|CAI]] commercial operations in Nurra.

As of 2026, the company has not yet released commercial varieties. Its first disease-resistant coffee lines are in field trials in Jala, with initial results expected by 2027. Drought-tolerant sugar cane and rice lines are in earlier-stage greenhouse testing.

== Technology ==

Genètica de l'Istme uses conventional and marker-assisted breeding techniques rather than {{w|genetic engineering}}:

* '''Marker-assisted selection''': Using {{w|DNA marker|genetic markers}} to identify plants carrying desirable traits — disease resistance, drought tolerance, yield — without introducing foreign DNA. This approach produces varieties that are not classified as {{w|genetically modified organism|GMOs}}, avoiding regulatory barriers and consumer resistance in export markets.
* '''Genomic selection''': Using genome-wide DNA markers to predict the performance of new varieties before field testing, reducing the time and cost of breeding cycles.
* '''Germplasm collection''': The company maintains a collection of Balboan crop varieties and wild relatives, sourced from cooperative farms, the university's agricultural research station in Jala, and CAI's commercial operations. This local germplasm is the basis for the company's breeding programmes, as it is already adapted to Balboan growing conditions.

== Operations ==

Genètica de l'Istme operates from a single facility at [[Plastic Beach]]:

* '''Laboratory and office''' (Dàrsena, Sant Cristòfor): A converted warehouse of approximately 600 square metres, housing the company's plant genetics laboratory, greenhouse, and offices. The greenhouse is used for early-stage seedling screening and controlled-environment testing. Approximately 35 employees.
* '''Field trial sites''': The company conducts field trials at cooperative farms in [[Jala Province|Jala]] (coffee, cacao) and [[Migjorn Province|Migjorn]] (sugar cane, rice), and at CAI commercial operations in [[Nurra Province|Nurra]] (palm oil, cattle forage).

== Ownership ==

Genètica de l'Istme is a private company. The ownership structure reflects its origin as a university spin-off with strategic agricultural investment:

* '''Founders''': 35% — Dr. Marta Vergés i Puig and Dr. Oriol Bosch i Riera
* '''[[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] (FIDB)''': 20% — sovereign wealth fund, seed investor
* '''[[Nutrició del Món]] (NDM)''': 20% — state-owned fertiliser and agricultural inputs company, strategic investor
* '''University of Sant Cristòfor Investment Fund''': 10% — university venture fund, seed investor
* '''Venture capital investors''': 15%

